## Exercise media — deliberately NOT redistributed

The upstream repository also contains `images/` and `videos/`. Per that
repository's own `LICENSE` (MEDIA EXCEPTION) and `NOTICE.md`, that media is:

    Copyright : © Gym Visual — https://gymvisual.com/
    Licence   : NOT covered by the MIT grant above

The upstream project states that cloning its repository grants no licence to
the media and that you must obtain your own licence directly from Gym Visual.

Accordingly, IronLog ships **none** of it. `scripts/build-exercise-data.mjs`
strips the `image`, `gif_url`, `media_id` and `attribution` fields from every
record, and fails closed if any media reference appears in its output. The unit
test `tests/catalogue.test.js` re-asserts this against the committed artefacts,
so a future regeneration cannot silently reintroduce media.

No exercise in IronLog displays an image, GIF or video. Exercises are presented
as text plus taxonomy.

